Pharmacol Rev</source><volume>55</volume><fpage>27</fpage><lpage>55</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">12615953</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="pone.0003296-Dagan1"><label>8</label><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Dagan</surname><given-names>A</given-names></name><name><surname>Efron</surname><given-names>L</given-names></name><name><surname>Gaidukov</surname><given-names>L</given-names></name><name><surname>Mor</surname><given-names>A</given-names></name><name><surname>Ginsburg</surname><given-names>H</given-names></name></person-group><year>2002</year><article-title>In vitro anti-<italic>Plasmodium</italic> effects of dermaseptin S4 derivatives.</article-title><source>Antimicrobial Agents Chemotherapy.</source><volume>46</volume><fpage>1059</fpage><lpage>1066</lpage></citation></ref><ref id="pone.0003296-Efron1"><label>9</label><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Efron</surname><given-names>L</given-names></name><name><surname>Dagan</surname><given-names>A</given-names></name><name><surname>Gaidukov</surname><given-names>L</given-names></name><name><surname>Mor</surname><given-names>A</given-names></name></person-group><year>2002</year><article-title>Direct interaction of dermaseptin S4 aminoheptanoyl derivative with intraerythrocitic malaria parasite leading to increased specific antiparasitic activity in culture.</article-title><source>JBC.</source><volume>277</volume><fpage>24067</fpage><lpage>24072</lpage></citation></ref><ref id="pone.0003296-WHO1"><label>10</label><citation citation-type="other"><collab>WHO</collab><year>2005</year><article-title>Word malaria report 2005. World Heath Organization. Geneva Switzerland.</article-title><comment>Available from: <ext-link ext-link-type="uri" xlink:href="http://www.rbm.who.int/wmr2005">http://www.rbm.who.int/wmr2005</ext-link></comment></citation></ref><ref id="pone.0003296-Gardner1"><label>11</label><cit